# The lockfile at the repo root is the project's own baseline and is
# intentionally NOT ignored — it is committed and tracked, so a clone
# keeps the dogfood baseline and `git status` shows its drift.
# No lockfile pattern is listed here on purpose: example lockfiles
# (e.g. examples/pr-review/skill-lock.json) stay committable too.
